1. THE PINS ON THE SUN (nature's numbers): k = G M / (r c^2) at the limb, the deflection 4 k, the Shapiro delay's coefficient 2 G M / c^3
   k at the limb = 2.122e-06; Newton's deflection 2 k = 0.876 arcsec; Einstein's 4 k = 1.751 arcsec (Dyson, Eddington and Davidson 1920: 1.98 +- 0.16 and 1.61 +- 0.40; VLBI: gamma = 0.99992 +- 0.00012, Lambert and Le Poncin-Lafitte 2011)
   the Shapiro delay at Cassini's geometry (Earth at 1 au, Saturn at 8.43 au, the ray at 1.6 solar radii): (2 G M / c^3) ln(4 r_1 r_2 / b^2) = 131 microseconds; Cassini's gamma - 1 = (2.1 +- 2.3) x 10^-5 (Bertotti, Iess and Tortora 2003)
   the second-order redshift: nature's 1 + z = 1 / sqrt(1 - 2 k) = 1 + k + (3 / 2) k^2 + (5 / 2) k^3 ...; the law today 1 + z = 1 + k exactly (the clock at 1 / (1 + k), 5.2)

